  data: {
    LLM: "Don't 'Call' cards in the early rounds unless it completes your Eye/Set. The penalty cards accumulate fast and can leave you with too many points if you don't go out first.\n\nWatch the 'Aces'. Black Aces (15) are dangerous to hold, but Red Aces (1) are excellent for lowering your point total if you are caught with cards at the end.\n\nThe 'Bending' Rule: If you go 'Down and Out' (meld your entire hand in one turn), your opponents score double points for their remaining cards. Try to time your melds to achieve this.",
    Player: "Don't 'Call' cards in the early rounds unless it completes your Eye/Set. The penalty cards accumulate fast and can leave you with too many points if you don't go out first.\n\nWatch the 'Aces'. Black Aces (15) are dangerous to hold, but Red Aces (1) are excellent for lowering your point total if you are caught with cards at the end.\n\nThe 'Bending' Rule: If you go 'Down and Out' (meld your entire hand in one turn), your opponents score double points for their remaining cards. Try to time your melds to achieve this.",
    aggressiveness: 0.5,
